# 🧪 Playwright E2E Tests

This project uses **[Playwright](https://playwright.dev)** for end-to-end (E2E) testing.  
You can run tests either **locally** (via Node.js) or inside a **Docker container** for fully reproducible results.  
The test suite also runs automatically in **GitHub Actions CI** on every pull request.

---

## ⚙️ Local Setup (Node.js)

Run Playwright tests locally if you have Node.js installed.

### 1️⃣ Prerequisites

Make sure you have the following installed:
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) **v18 or later**
- **npm v8 or later**

### 2️⃣ Install dependencies

```bash
npm ci
```

### 3️⃣ Install Playwright browsers and system dependencies

```bash
npx playwright install --with-deps
```

### 4️⃣ Run tests locally

```bash
npx playwright test
```

### 5️⃣ View the HTML report

After your tests complete, generate and open the test report:

```bash
npx playwright show-report
```

Or manually open the generated file:

```
playwright-report/index.html
```

---

## 🐳 Run Tests via Docker

Running tests in Docker ensures consistent behavior across different environments — perfect for CI pipelines and team collaboration.

### 1️⃣ Build the Docker image

```bash
docker build -t playwright-tests .
```

### 2️⃣ Run Playwright tests inside the container

```bash
docker run --rm -v $(pwd)/playwright-report:/app/playwright-report playwright-tests
```

> 💡 The `-v` flag mounts your local `playwright-report` folder so reports are saved on your machine.

### 3️⃣ View the HTML report

After the test run completes, open the report locally:

```
./playwright-report/index.html
```

---

## 🧭 CI Integration (GitHub Actions)

This project includes a **GitHub Actions workflow** (`.github/workflows/playwright.yml`) that:

1. Builds the Docker image  
2. Runs Playwright tests  
3. Uploads the HTML report as a downloadable artifact  

> You can view test results and download the report directly from the **GitHub Actions → Artifacts** section after a workflow run.

---

## 🧰 Useful Commands

| Command | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `npx playwright test` | Run all tests locally |
| `npx playwright test --ui` | Run tests in interactive UI mode |
| `npx playwright show-report` | Open the last HTML report |
| `npx playwright codegen <url>` | Generate tests by recording browser actions |
| `npx playwright test --grep "keyword"` | Run only tests matching a keyword |

